<!-- Wrapper to allow easy inclusion of layout -->
<%- include('../layout', { body: '' }) %>
<!-- Note: EJS implementation usually includes the layout at the end or uses 'extend' logic. 
     For simplicity in this structure, I will assume the individual views contain the content 
     and are wrapped by the layout logic in the response or via specific EJS libraries.
     However, standard EJS is simple include. 
     
     CORRECTION: To make this robust without extra libs, I will define the views to just be the content
     and pass them into the layout during res.render if I used a layout middleware. 
     
     But the Spring way wraps fragments. 
     The standard Node way: 
     1. Include Header
     2. Content
     3. Include Footer
-->
